   "evidence": "Lines 72-110 contain no `sphericalBesselJ` occurrence (grep for `sphericalBessel` in the file first matches at line 114). Mathlib has no equivalent: grep `\u2200\u1da0 .* in cocompact` over `upstream/mathlib/Mathlib` returns only `Topology/Order/Compact.lean` order-extremum lemmas and `Analysis/Complex/PhragmenLindelof.lean:677`, and `inv_mul_inv_eq` has no match \u2014 so these are new general lemmas, not restatements of existing public API. Per the PR description, \u00a70.4 and the \u00a75.3 phase shifts work in the same cocompact/Riccati vocabulary and would need them.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/SpecialFunctions/SphericalBessel/Asymptotics.lean",
   "fix": "Relocate them, public, to a Mathlib-mirrored module (e.g. `EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Analysis/Asymptotics/Cocompact.lean`, the way `Mathematics/Topology/Algebra/GroupWithZero.lean` already carries `ContinuousAt.eq_zero_of_forall_id_mul_eq_zero` for `SphericalBessel/Basic.lean`), stating them at their natural generality (proper normed field for the `inv` lemmas). Keep only the genuinely argument-specific `sin_sub_add_two_mul_pi_div_two` and `isBigO_inv_of_isBigO_mul_sub_sin` private here; `inv_mul_inv_eq_inv_sq` may instead be inlined.",
